# Trivy ignore list for the irs-api image scan (.github/workflows/trivy-image-scan.yml).
# The scan fails on any HIGH or CRITICAL finding that is not listed here.

# spring-webmvc 6.2.19: fixed only in Spring Framework 7.0.9, no fix available in the 6.2 line.
# Affects XsltView, which the IRS does not use.
# Re-review with the upgrade to Spring Framework 7.
CVE-2026-47884

# spring-webmvc 6.2.19: fixed in Spring Framework 7.0.9, the 6.2.20 fix is not available as open source.
# Affects view fragments sent over Server-Sent Events, which the IRS does not use.
# Re-review with the upgrade to Spring Framework 7.
CVE-2026-47890

# libexpat 2.9.0-r0 from the pinned eclipse-temurin:25-jre-alpine base image, fixed in 2.10.0-r0.
# Denial of service while parsing XML. In the image only fontconfig uses libexpat, to read its own
# configuration; the IRS parses XML with the JDK and does not render fonts.
# Re-review with the next update of the pinned base image (Alpine 3.24.4 ships the fixed version).
CVE-2026-113351
CVE-2026-115506
CVE-2026-117610
CVE-2026-118370

# libfontenc 1.1.9-r0 from the pinned eclipse-temurin:25-jre-alpine base image, fixed in 1.1.10-r0.
# Font file parsing. In the image only mkfontscale uses libfontenc; the IRS neither runs it nor reads font files.
# Re-review with the next update of the pinned base image (Alpine 3.24.4 ships the fixed version).
CVE-2026-109908
